---
import HeroProducts from '@/components/HeroProducts.astro'
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const page = {
 title: 'Screen Printing vs Embroidery for Construction Gear',
 description:
 'Compare screen printing and embroidery by garment, artwork, quantity, care, intended use, manufacturer instructions, and written quote.',
 url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/screen-printing-vs-embroidery-construction-las-vegas/',
}

const compare = [
 { row: 'T-shirts and long sleeves', options: 'Print or embroidery', review: 'Print is the usual pick, especially for large logos and big runs' },
 { row: 'Polos and button-downs', options: 'Print or embroidery', review: 'Embroidery is the usual pick for client-facing roles' },
 { row: 'Hats and caps', options: 'Embroidery, patch, or transfer', review: 'Embroidery is the usual pick, and a patch can carry finer detail' },
 { row: 'Jackets and softshells', options: 'Embroidery, print, or transfer', review: 'Check the shell, since needles and heat can harm waterproof fabric' },
 { row: 'Hi-vis and protective apparel', options: 'Product-specific review', review: 'Follow the garment maker’s instructions for method and placement' },
]

const faqs = [
 { q: 'Should I use screen printing or embroidery for construction gear?', a: 'Use screen printing for crew tees and big back prints, and embroidery for polos, jackets, and hats. If you’re unsure, send your logo and we’ll price both.' },
 { q: 'Which method lasts longer?', a: 'Embroidery often outlasts a print on heavy garments, but thread can snag. A well-cured print on a good tee holds up well too. The washing routine matters for both.' },
 { q: 'Which method costs less?', a: 'Screen printing usually costs less on larger runs of simple art. Embroidery can compare better on small orders. Send your logo and count and we’ll price both.' },
 { q: 'Can you decorate FR or arc-rated shirts?', a: 'Only after the employer and garment manufacturer approve the exact product, materials, method, size, and placement.' },
 { q: 'Can decoration affect ANSI/ISEA 107 apparel?', a: 'Yes. Decoration can affect required background or reflective material. Review the exact garment and scaled proof with the employer and manufacturer.' },
 { q: 'Can one order include both methods?', a: 'Yes. Printed tees and embroidered polos can go on the same quote.' },
]

const breadcrumb = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
 itemListElement: [
  { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' },
  { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Screen Printing vs Embroidery for Construction', item: page.url },
 ],
}

const faqSchema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@type': 'FAQPage',
 mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: faq.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.a } })),
}

const articleSchema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@type': 'Article',
 headline: 'Screen Printing vs Embroidery for Construction Gear in Las Vegas',
 description: page.description,
 author: { '@id': 'https://bighornthreads.com/#organization' },
 publisher: { '@id': 'https://bighornthreads.com/#organization' },
 mainEntityOfPage: page.url,
 datePublished: '2026-07-08',
 dateModified: '2026-08-21',
}
---

<BaseLayout title={page.title} description={page.description} canonical={page.url}>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumb)} />
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

 <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-concrete pt-16 pb-20 sm:pb-28">
  <div class="page-hero-grid relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-ash" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-700">Home</a><span class="px-2 text-ash">/</span><span class="text-gold-700">Screen Printing vs Embroidery</span>
   </nav>
   <p class="kicker mb-4">Decoration Methods</p>
   <h1 class="mb-6 max-w-4xl font-heading text-4xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-[1.0] tracking-tight text-charcoal sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">Screen printing vs embroidery for construction gear</h1>
   <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash sm:text-xl">Print the crew tees and big back logos. Stitch the polos, jackets, and hats. For hi-vis and FR, start with what the garment maker allows.</p>
   <div class="mt-10"><a href="/get-a-quote/" class="btn-primary text-base">Get a Quote</a></div>
   <HeroProducts />
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-paper py-14">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <p class="speakable-answer text-xl leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-2xl">Screen printing lays ink on the fabric, so it suits big logos and larger runs. Embroidery builds the logo with thread, so it looks finished up close on heavier garments.</p>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="bg-concrete py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <div class="mb-10 max-w-2xl">
    <p class="kicker mb-3">Method by Garment</p>
    <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">The usual pick by garment</h2>
   </div>
   <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-hairline bg-panel">
    <table class="w-full min-w-[720px]">
     <thead class="bg-paper"><tr class="border-b border-hairline">
      <th class="px-6 py-4 text-left font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gold-600">Garment</th>
      <th class="px-6 py-4 text-left font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gold-600">Possible Methods</th>
      <th class="px-6 py-4 text-left font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gold-600">Review</th>
     </tr></thead>
     <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
      {compare.map((row) => (
       <tr>
        <td class="px-6 py-5 align-top font-mono text-sm font-bold text-gold-700">{row.row}</td>
        <td class="px-6 py-5 align-top font-heading text-base font-bold text-charcoal">{row.options}</td>
        <td class="px-6 py-5 align-top text-sm text-ash">{row.review}</td>
       </tr>
      ))}
     </tbody>
    </table>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="border-y border-hairline bg-paper py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <p class="kicker mb-3">The Buyer's Review</p>
   <h2 class="mb-8 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Compare the complete order</h2>
   <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
    <div><h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Garment and artwork</h3><p>Small type and thin lines lose out in thread, and stretchy fabric puckers under it. Ask for a proof on the actual garment.</p></div>
    <div><h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Quantity and price</h3><p>Printing gets cheaper per piece as the run grows, and ink colors add setup. Embroidery is priced more by stitch count, so it tends to compare better on small runs.</p></div>
    <div><h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Use and care</h3><p>On a job site, abrasion and hard washing wear out both. Choose a heavy garment first, and follow the care instructions.</p></div>
    <div><h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Protective apparel</h3><p>On hi-vis, FR, or arc-rated gear, the garment maker sets which methods, materials, and placements are allowed.</p></div>
    <div><h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Written terms</h3><p>Your quote lists the products, sizes, price, and timing before you approve.</p></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="bg-concrete py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <h2 class="mb-8 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
   <div class="space-y-5">
    {faqs.map((faq) => (
     <div class="border border-hairline bg-panel p-6">
      <h3 class="mb-3 font-heading text-lg font-bold text-charcoal">{faq.q}</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-ash">{faq.a}</p>
     </div>
    ))}
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="border-t border-hairline bg-navy-950 py-16 text-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-center sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <h2 class="mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Compare methods for your actual order</h2>
   <p class="mb-8 text-lg text-navy-200">Send your garment list, logo, and how many of each.</p>
   <a href="/get-a-quote/" class="btn-primary text-base">Get a Quote</a>
  </div>
 </section>
</BaseLayout>
